  "method": "Autocorrelation function of 2 m temperature forecast error, by lag in hours, per lead day. acf[L-1] is the plain lag-L autocorrelation over every pair of hours exactly L hours apart, L = 1 .. 30, taken about the series mean. Each lead is then fitted with a four-component unit-variance process: a trip-wide flat offset, a 24 h harmonic, a 12 h harmonic, a stationary AR(1) in absolute clock time, and hour-to-hour white noise, so that rho(L) = w_shared + w_diurnal*cos(2pi L/24) + w_semidiurnal*cos(2pi L/12) + w_ar*phi^L. Weighted least squares on lags 1 .. 24 (weight 4 on the lags a phase window sees, 1 to 9, and on lag 24, weight 1 elsewhere), subject to non-negative shares summing to at most 1. The legacy exchangeable shares (tripVarianceFraction, nightVarianceFraction, hourVarianceFraction, from rho_within_night at lags <= 9 h) are still computed and kept readable, but they collapse a decaying and sign-changing autocorrelation into one number and are no longer consumed.",
